[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SSDD001
TITLE: Airport, local computers, and neighbor topology, with the two failure domains
STATEMENT: >>>
The system design shall separate two failure domains. Inside an airport, n computers share one ordered log and lose the authority only when they lose a majority. Between airports, a link failure isolates the airports and each continues with local service under the fail-smart rule. A local computer failure shall not be treated as a neighbor-link failure, and a neighbor-link failure shall not by itself remove a local majority. Acceptance is a design trace that names both domains and a test in which a down neighbor leaves the local majority able to clear a local aircraft.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The two domains fail differently. Mixing them would either stop a healthy local tower or keep using a dead neighbor.
<<<
DAL: A
REQUIREMENT_LEVEL: Low-Level
VERIFICATION: Review
ASSUMPTIONS: The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment. Raft is assumed to deliver one ordered log and is not re-proved.
